        <headline>Flood Warning issued September 23 at 9:05PM CDT until September 26 at 9:00PM CDT by NWS Quad Cities IA IL</headline>
        <description>...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Iowa...

Iowa River near Lone Tree affecting Washington, Johnson and Louisa
Counties.

English River at Kalona affecting Washington and Johnson Counties.

Cedar River near Conesville affecting Muscatine and Louisa
Counties.

Iowa River at Oakville affecting Louisa County.

Iowa River at Wapello affecting Louisa County.

* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring.

* WHERE...Iowa River at Wapello.

* WHEN...Until Saturday evening.

* IMPACTS...At 22.0 feet, Water affects residences near the U.S.
Highway 61 bridge.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 8:00 PM CDT Wednesday the stage was 23.7 feet.
- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending
at 8:00 PM CDT Wednesday was 23.8 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage early
Saturday afternoon and continue falling to 16.4 feet Wednesday,
September 30.
- Flood stage is 21.0 feet.
</description>
        <instruction>

Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.

Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars
through flooded areas.

Caution is urged when walking near riverbanks.

The next statement will be issued by late tonight.</instruction>
